---
id: PY-012
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'yaml.load without a SafeLoader, or from pickle import loads'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 9

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(call) @target'

related: [PY-009]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

The regex tier cannot tell `yaml.load(src, Loader=SafeLoader)` from a bare
`yaml.load(src)`. This gate-time companion fires on `yaml.load(` /
`yaml.full_load(` without a `Loader=` that is `SafeLoader` or `CSafeLoader`,
and on `loads(` reached via `from pickle import loads`.

`yaml.safe_load(` stays clean. Same-line `yaml.load(src, Loader=SafeLoader)` is
clean here (PY-009 regex may still fire — documented, suppressible; this rule
does not rewrite PY-009). `os.system` / `shell=True` stay regex PY-009.
